sue, but so does dropping <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">mu_x + gamma_wx*w</span> (and relevant parameter stuff) and replacing it with 0.  Even dropping both yields the same, so it&#39;s got to be <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">x</span> itself.  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">x</span> doesn&#39;t have any NA values though (values: <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462237341000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1WppggQnOtuR9xqme_jp_3\">https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R</a>), and R&#39;s <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">dnorm</span> works fine on it.  It would be great if someone could help me out here.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Josh.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
