    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Mar 2, 2020 at 4:21 AM &#39;Josh&#39; via TMB Users &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">tmb-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello,</div><div><br></div>I&#39;m trying to estimate <i>∫</i>f(lw)*f(x,y | exp(lw))dw, where f(lw) is an already-estimated mixture model (using mclust).  However, I keep getting &quot;NA/NaN function evaluation&quot; from nlminb and I&#39;m not quite sure exactly why.<div><br></div><div>R code:<br><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><div>library(TMB)<br>library(mclust)<br>dw &lt;- densityMclust(log(w_o))</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>parameters &lt;- list(</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>lw = rep(0, length(y)),</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>gamma_wy = -0.7,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>gamma_wxy = -0.7,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>gamma_wx = -0.7,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>lsigma_y = -0.7,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>lsigma_x = -0.7,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>mu_y = 0,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>mu_x = 0,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>b = 0</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>data &lt;- list(</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>x = x,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>y = y,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>dw_mean = dw$parameters$mean,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>dw_prop = dw$parameters$pro,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>dw_sigma = sqrt(dw$parameters$variance$sigmasq)</div><div>)<br><br><div>compile(&quot;file.cpp&quot;)</div><div>dyn.load(dynlib(&quot;file&quot;))</div><div>obj &lt;- MakeADFun(</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>data=data, parameters=parameters,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DLL=&quot;file&quot;,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>random=c(&quot;lw&quot;)</div><div>)</div><div><br></div><div>opt &lt;- nlminb(obj$par, obj$fn, obj$gr)</div></div></font></div></code></div><br>Then, in C++/TMB:</div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><div><font color=\"#660066\">#include &lt;TMB.hpp&gt;</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">template&lt;class Type&gt;</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">vector&lt;Type&gt; dw(vector&lt;Type&gt; lw, vector&lt;Type&gt; means, vector&lt;Type&gt; prop, vector&lt;Type&gt; sigma)</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">{</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>vector&lt;Type&gt; res(lw.size());</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>for (int i = 0; i &lt; lw.size(); i++)</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>{</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t\t</span>res(i) = 0;</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t\t</span>for (int j = 0; j &lt; means.size(); j++)</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t\t</span>{</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t\t\t</span>res(i) += prop(j)*dnorm(lw(i), means(j), sigma(j), false);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t\t</span>}</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>}</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>return log(res);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">}</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">template&lt;class Type&gt;</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">Type objective_function&lt;Type&gt;::operator() ()</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">{</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DATA_VECTOR(x);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DATA_VECTOR(y);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DATA_VECTOR(dw_mean);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DATA_VECTOR(dw_prop);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>DATA_VECTOR(dw_sigma);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER_VECTOR(lw);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(gamma_wy);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(gamma_wxy);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(gamma_wx);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(lsigma_y);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(lsigma_x);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(mu_y);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(mu_x);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>PARAMETER(b);</font></div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"><font color=\"#660066\">\t</font></span></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>vector&lt;Type&gt; w = exp(lw);</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>Type nll = -dw(lw, dw_mean, dw_prop, dw_sigma).sum();</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>nll -= dnorm(y,</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">              mu_y + b*x + gamma_wy*w + gamma_wxy*w*x,</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">              exp(lsigma_y), true).sum();</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>nll -= dnorm(x,</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">              mu_x + gamma_wx*w,</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">              exp(lsigma_x), true).sum();</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span>return nll;</font></div><div><font color=\"#660066\">}</font></div><div><br></div></div></code></div><br></div><div>The original <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">w_o</span> are distributed as Beta(2,5), and the <i>prop</i> values sum to 1.  The issue doesn&#39;t seem to be in <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">dw</span> or <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">exp(lw)</span>, as removing them doesn&#39;t stop the problem.  It actually seems to be in the <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">dnorm</span> call for x, as the issue does go away when it&#39;s removed, but I can&#39;t figure out why.  Dropping <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">lsigma_x</span> (and relevant parameter stuff) and just using 1 for the variance gives the same issue, but so does dropping <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">mu_x + gamma_wx*w</span> (and relevant parameter stuff) and replacing it with 0.  Even dropping both yields the same, so it&#39;s got to be <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">x</span> itself.  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace\">x</span> doesn&#39;t have any NA values though (values: <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462237346000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1RJfnAKlTKhYq0PHAMXS6J\">https://pastebin.com/vv50R82R</a>), and R&#39;s <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102);font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">dnorm</span> works fine on it.  It would be great if someone could help me out here.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you,</div><div>Josh.</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">us...@tmb-project.org</a>. Before posting, please check the wiki and issuetracker at <a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462237346000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0venFOLtnEJzOXIYzLljkl\">https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/</a>. Please try to create a simple repeatable example to go with your question (e.g issues 154, 134, 51). Use the issuetracker to report bugs.<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;TMB Users&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
